invariant: INV-17
file: src/chacha20.c
catches: chacha20_wipe_test
reason: a device object's chacha20_xor returns without the wipe of the
  stack below it, so the dead frames of its body keep the state, whose
  words 4 to 11 are the key. Every byte it writes is still right.
  bin/chacha20_wipe_test copies the stack below a call and looks for the
  key.

--- old
    xor_body(key, nonce, counter, in, out, n);
    wipe_frame_call();
--- new
    xor_body(key, nonce, counter, in, out, n);
